// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Scanner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P657941087" "The Tac-Scanner"
// DetailString :
"P77065661" "Two recon patrols from the Compound have went missing in the tunnels of the Forlorn. Luckily, the second patrol had a tracer-beacon with them. The tac-scanner the Hetman gave you should help track down their whereabouts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Sabotage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1204682740" "Scheming on a Thing"
// DetailString :
"P3544547193" "The controls to the Forlorn's outer gate seals are surprisingly advanced...and certainly too complex for the <color red>Ghouls</color> to have activated on their own. Someone else caused the breach. The Palatine is correct. Something doesn't add up."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Coup 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3096013207" "A Sudden and Decisive Action"
// DetailString :
"P3510720836" "During your battle with the Kill Team Leader, he boasted that the Hetman wasn't just cleaning house at the meeting spot, but at the Compound as well! That means anyone the Hetman sees as an enemy is going to be lined up and shot...including the Palatine and the Carnival prisoners. <color orange>You've got to get back to the Compound and stop him!</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ShaleInJail 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P279922102" "Forlorn Justice: Shale"
// DetailString :
"P3153613152" "You have left one of the Hetman's recon team, Shale, in the custody of the Forlorn."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BiddleInJail 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2453149336" "Forlorn Justice: Biddle"
// DetailString :
"P2508737670" "You have left one of the Hetman's recon team, Biddle, in the custody of the Forlorn."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SavedNone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2839086534" "Topsiders Never Learn"
// DetailString :
"P2042948907" "The fight with the Forlorn was a massacre. All of the Hetman's recon team are dead."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P836527009" "Abused and Scorned Tho' We May Be"
// DetailString :
"P3644738134" "Though the dying Monarch had passed along the rulership of First Ward's Survivor Compound to Anna Palatine, her title went unrecognized by the bloody-minded Hetman."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3619211523" "Though the dying Monarch had passed along the rulership of First Ward's Survivor Compound to Anna Palatine, her title went unrecognized by the bloody-minded Hetman. To gather allies and win the support of the people of the Compound, an alliance was forged with the Forlorn and another <i>re-forged</i> with the Carnival of Light."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - AnnaPalatineSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P484926789" "And it came to pass that Anna Palatine claimed her birthright…<br><br><b><color deepskyblue>Abused and Scorned Tho' We May Be</color></b><br><br>Though the dying Monarch had passed along the rulership of First Ward's Survivor Compound to Anna Palatine, her title went unrecognized by the bloody-minded Hetman. To gather allies and win the support of the people of the Compound, an alliance was forged with the Forlorn and another <i>re-forged</i> with the Carnival of Light. The Hetman staged a military coup to prevent any of this from happening but, in the end, he was undone."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HetmanPreForlornDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1018778064" "{HeroName}, have you come to convince me to let your Carnival friends go again?"
// Answer Text :
"P3913099066" "The Palatine already made that command. You're still ignoring it."
// Page NoWay Text :
"P992019164" "The only command that I am <i>ignoring</i> is the last one given by a Monarch who wasn't in his right mind.<br><br>I don't trust that girl, I don't trust how she magically appeared, and I'm beginning not to trust you, {HeroName}. Now speak your mind or go back to the gumbo."
// Answer Text :
"P664815989" "The Palatine says you've been having trouble with the Forlorn."
// Page ForlornHelp Text :
"P1665440816" "And let me guess: you want to help me out. Wait. Silly me, let's say that again with the Color Obvious turned on: the so-called Palatine wants to make a gesture both to me and the people of Last Word by helping out with the <color red>Ghoul</color> problem.<br><br>And you're her running dog, making sure it all transpires."
// Answer Text :
"P4129576911" "Paranoid much? I'm just here to help."
// Answer Text :
"P95751165" "And you're going to look like a fool for declining my help."
// Page HetmanAcceptsHelp Text :
"P3798828066" "<color deepskyblue>Abused and Scorned Tho' We May Be</color><br><br><color deepskyblue>Part Two: Haters Gonna Hate</color><br><br><b>*sigh*</b><br><br> I <b>do</b> need the help. Listen. <color red>These 'Forlorn' aren't like any Ghouls you may have encountered before. They're more disciplined, able to show a measure of tactical acumen on the battlefield.</color><br><br>If you're detecting a hint of admiration in my voice, it's because you're missing my point completely. The Forlorn are still monsters. Don't forget that. The fact that they can think only makes them worse."
// Answer Text :
"P3216830559" "I can handle them."
// Page ReconLost Text :
"P884987116" "Good to hear, because the last recon patrol I sent out to check on them certainly couldn't. They went into the tunnels outside the Compound and vanished."
// Answer Text :
"P4220005699" "Wait, why were you sending recon patrols into the Forlorn tunnels in the first place?"
// Page MovingOut Text :
"P3557871365" "Remember when we first met, {HeroName}? <color red>D.U.S.T.<color> was poking its nose around too close to the Compound and I had <i>you</i> deal with it. Same story here. It's called keeping tabs on your enemy, genius. While you're playing fetch for that ineffectual, high-talkin' little Shepherd girl, I'm still making sure we're <i>all</i> protected.<br><br>Here. The recon patrol had a portable tracer-beacon with them. This tac-scanner will hone in on their trail. <color orange>Find whatever is left of my people and...<i> take care</i> of any Forlorn you encounter.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3366905474" "I'll find them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - WardenDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskOwnerPage Text :
"P1917510563" "<color orange>Only your team leader may speak to the Warden</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page AlreadyTalked Text :
"P3629845417" "Just remember you said you'd be cool. We don't want any more trouble. We've got enough of that already. But if violence somehow breaks out, we're going to hold you responsible."
// Page FirstTalk Text :
"P818436738" "Okay, everyone just stop! There's been enough violence in these last few days.<br><br>And you? You stay <i>right</i> there, topsider. You've got the smell of the gumbo on you... but only slightly. You're a newcomer, but I won't ask what brought you here...or, more likely, who <i>forced</i> you into First Ward. That's your own business.<br><br>I <i>will</i> ask, though, what brings you down into our tunnels. The last few visitors we had...well, they weren't willing to answer that. They were too busy trying to pump us full of lead...<br><br>...buncha so-called 'recon soldiers' from the Compound. More of a <i>kill team</i> , the way they acted. You know 'em?'"
// Answer Text :
"P3631547547" "That's who I'm looking for. And I mean you no harm."
// Answer Text :
"P2120578896" "That's who I'm looking for. Now stand aside or I'll put you down."
// Page Peaceful Text :
"P557026664" "Between you and me, the Forlorn have bigger troubles than keeping Compound yahoos captive, so I'll make you a deal. We'll stay here all peaceful-like until you do something <i>uncool</i>.<br><br>You can speak to the recon soldiers we have locked up. You can even free them if you want. It's your call. But if <i>any of them</i> do something uncool, then we're going to hold you responsible. Which is to say, we'll beat you down.<br><br>And <color orange>choose carefully</color> which ones you want to save. The ones named <color red>Shale</color> and <color red>Biddle</color> are itching for a rematch with us."
// Answer Text :
"P4262229902" "Understood."
// Page Aggro Text :
"P3497286551" "You're just like <i>them</i>. See a former <color red>Ghoul<color>, jump for the throat. But, hey, I gave you a chance."
// Answer Text :
"P2743070784" "(Finish him and swipe the prison keys)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ShaleDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page WeGottaMove Text :
"P630751227" "What's going on outside?"
// Answer Text :
"P878766664" "Come with me. This place is no longer safe."
// Page ShaleHatesYou Text :
"P795163754" "Come to change your mind about me? Don't bother. I'd rather stay down here with these beauty queens than deal with traitorous scum like you."
// Answer Text :
"P2507754309" "Have it your way."
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P1605536580" "You're from the Compound? Who sent you?"
// Answer Text :
"P3199422367" "Long story. Are you hurt?"
// Page Choice Text :
"P2878136548" "Not at all. The Forlorn were real gentlemen. <color red>But as soon as you get me out of here, I'm going to punch their faces in.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2930974875" "Nice. You're a chump and a troublemaker. You deserve to stay locked up."
// Answer Text :
"P1761679774" "Sounds like a plan. Let me get you out of here."
// Page StayInJail Text :
"P2524576575" "What?! Are you <i>crazy</i> or something?! If you're siding with the Ghouls instead of the Hetman then you can bite me, chomper. Thanks for nothing."
// Answer Text :
"P2659859680" "Enjoy your stay. The Compound doesn't need loose cannons like you."
// Page GoFree Text :
"P474381884" "Let's get 'em!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - BiddleDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page WeGottaMove Text :
"P3165323769" "What's up?"
// Answer Text :
"P1369347861" "Grab your gear. The Forlorn are out for blood."
// Page BiddleHatesYou Text :
"P3988671160" "{Hero.gender=male Boy|Girl}, I already told you to get outta my face. I'll wait until the Hetman sends someone that doesn't wanna paint pretty rainbows with <color red>Ghouls</color>."
// Answer Text :
"P2362584480" "Suit yourself."
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P3572011210" "Did the Hetman send you?"
// Answer Text :
"P2337431490" "He and the Palatine both did. How are you holding up?"
// Page Choice Text :
"P3415180814" "<i>HOW AM I HOLDING UP?!</i><br><br>I'm sitting in a <color>Ghoul</color> cell. Er, sorry, a <i>Forlorn</i> cell. Same difference. What, are you their spokeman or something? <color red>Well, here's how it's going to work: you're going to let me out and <i>I'm</i> to carry out my orders. Which are simple: kill these scumbags.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2989804294" "That's exactly the sort of nonsense I don't need right now. You're staying here."
// Answer Text :
"P897489108" "Let's do it."
// Page StayInJail Text :
"P2878751088" "If you're not going to help me wipe the floor with these monsters, then stay outta my face. Shove off, chomper."
// Answer Text :
"P771275626" "Keep talking. Maybe a few years down here will cool your jets, tough guy."
// Page GoFree Text :
"P2497053388" "That's the spirit! Back on mission!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - FalcoDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page WeGottaMove Text :
"P3544413785" "Come on. We need to get out of here."
// Page FalcoAppeal Text :
"P3257970427" "Hey, listen, please reconsider letting me out of here. I know we instigated this, but I never even opened fire. The Forlorn are the victims here, I get that, but it doesn't mean you have to condemn me to stay among them."
// Answer Text :
"P4153560831" "I'm going to think about it."
// Answer Text :
"P497483457" "We'll go back and tell the Hetman that. You're free."
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P1750946512" "Have you come from the Compound? Why aren't the Forlorn attacking you?"
// Answer Text :
"P1842087484" "I struck a deal with them. Are you all right?"
// Page Choice Text :
"P415635191" "I'm fine, considering the circumstances. The Forlorn haven't touched us since we were taken captive. I mean, yeah, they fought back when my team attacked them, but that's our fault.<br><br>We invaded their territory, thinking that they were bogeymen ready to pounce on us at any moment. But that isn't the case. They've got problems of their own. They never even <b>had</b> aspirations of moving in on the Compound. That was just the Hetman's own paranoia. We should have ignored his orders to come down here and just blindfire, you hear what I'm saying?<br><br>Are you going to let me get out of here?"
// Page StayInJail Text :
"P3758880118" "All right, but I'm telling you the truth about all of it. Just don't take too long to make up your mind, okay? I miss my family back topside."
// Page GoFree Text :
"P2829025816" "Thanks, {HeroName}! I'll stay at your side and won't cause any trouble. We've done enough to these poor creatures already."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TalbotDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page WeGottaMove Text :
"P4243244447" "Who are you? What's happened?"
// Answer Text :
"P304840711" "On your feet, soldier. We've got to move."
// Page TalbotAppeal Text :
"P2860536388" "{HeroName}, I'm beggin' you, let me out of here. The Forlorn obviously trust you enough that it's your call. And, yeah, speaking of making calls, I made a bad one. Namely, following the Hetman's orders without question. The Folorn aren't the bad guys, I realize that now. Don't make me out to be one, too."
// Answer Text :
"P620915242" "Fine, but keep your cool. I want us to get through this without violence."
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P2625799074" "{HeroName}, I recognize you from the Compound! Are you going to get us out of here?"
// Answer Text :
"P1014794627" "Some of you, maybe. How have the Forlorn been treating you?"
// Page Choice Text :
"P1660765010" "Well, it's prison, but I would've thought we'd be executed by now... considering that we came in and started shooting at them without warning. After they subdued us and threw us in these cells, it's been nothing but three meals a day. One of them even bandaged me up. We were wrong about them, {HeroName}, the Forlorn aren't evil. The fact that they're letting you decide my fate peacefully should be enough to prove that.<br><br>So are you going to let me out of here?"
// Answer Text :
"P4237289925" "Yes, but keep your cool. I want us to get through this without violence."
// Page StayInJail Text :
"P2671188282" "Okay, mull it over. I'm not innocent, I know that, but I'm not going to cause any trouble. I promise."
// Page GoFree Text :
"P449886117" "I was hoping you'd say that. Let's make a bee-line for the exit. I swear I won't cause any problems."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - GyreDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page WeGottaMove Text :
"P2322244457" "Let me out of here <i>now</i>!"
// Answer Text :
"P380833823" "The Forlorn are everywhere. Stay close."
// Answer Text :
"P2391404258" "Let's get out of here. And don't cause any trouble with the Forlorn."
// Page OpeningPage Text :
"P3685649598" "How'd you get past the Forlorn?"
// Answer Text :
"P2177182452" "Simple. I spoke to them reasonably. How are you feeling?"
// Page Choice Text :
"P2666265747" "I'm a little scared... who wouldn't be? I keep expecting the Forlorn to exact some revenge for our boneheaded attack on them, but it doesn't look like that's going to happen.<br><br>Look, {HeroName}, whatever we were told about the Forlorn was more of the Hetman getting as unhinged as the Monarch used to be. The Forlorn...they're just people. Scary-looking, used-to-be-cannibal people, but <i>people</i>, okay? And if you let me go back topside to the Compound, I'll spread the word. Even if it gets me thrown into <i>another</i> cell."
// Answer Text :
"P2852708861" "I'll get back to you on that."
// Page StayInJail Text :
"P2578819848" "<i>What?</i><br><br>C'mon, {HeroName}! Let me out of here! I won't make them angry, I swear!"
// Page GoFree Text :
"P1739188572" "Music to my ears. I'm gone."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HetmanPostForlornDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3381351683" "{HeroName}, give me a status report on the recon patrol that went into the tunnels."
// Answer Text :
"P2371784735" "I saved everyone that I could."
// Answer Text :
"P1709317830" "None of them made it back to the surface."
// Answer Text :
"P1524570425" "I brought the innocent ones back to the surface."
// Page SavedEveryone Text :
"P3853754694" "You have my genuine thanks. You really oughtta reconsider working for the witch girl and throw in your hat with me."
// Answer Text :
"P1170149083" "I stand by the Palatine. Goodbye, Hetman."
// Page SavedNone Text :
"P3949062238" "...<br><br>...<i>worthless</i>.<br><br>Get outta my face before I throw you in the clink with those Carnies."
// Answer Text :
"P1416374730" "You're welcome to try that anytime, Hetman. Goodbye."
// Page SavedInnocentOnes Text :
"P2856600275" "<b>'The innocent ones?'</b> Are you telling me you left some of my people down there with the <color red>Ghouls</color>..?!"
// Answer Text :
"P1615831308" "Only those unrepentent for their crimes against the Forlorn."
// Page DeservedIt Text :
"P1321136016" "Are you beyond insane?! Give me back that tac-scanner, you self-righteous dimwit! I'll send another team to finish the job!<br><br>You left them with monsters, {HeroName}. <b>Monsters.</b><br>Get out of my face."
// Answer Text :
"P476555902" "You're making a mistake, Hetman. Goodbye."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2940146656" "As you have seen, the Compound is a fragile bastion against the myriad evil running amok in First Ward. Though the Hetman will not admit it, we need to be fostering <i>more</i> alliances with those around us, not <i>alienating</i> the ones we already had. The Carnival of Light will not protect us again until we heal the schism that has risen between us. And we cannot heal that schism until my sovereignty is recognized. It's chess now with the Hetman, and I think I have found my next move.<br><br><color yellow>The Forlorn</color> live below us in the tunnels beneath the Compound. They are former <color red>Ghouls</color> who have had their minds restored through the efforts of Dr. Helix and other brave souls at the Battle of Neutropolis.<br><br>They are a pitiable folk, the Forlorn, trapped in their now-desiccated frames, remembering every hideous act they committed in the red-minded madness of their former affliction. They are pariahs, even here in First Ward. And they would make powerful friends. <color orange>Find the Hetman and convince him to let you to enter the tunnels and speak to the Forlorn.</color><br><br>He will bluster and mock my efforts to parley with them, but he will not deny you. The Compound is afraid of the Forlorn, thinking them monsters, and perhaps understandably so. But if word got out that the Hetman denied your help in dealing with them, he would lose face. Either way, I edge closer to the seat of my birthright."
// AcceptString :
"P1391961168" "I'll speak to the Hetman about the Forlorn"
// SendOffString :
"P2716747083" "My thanks, {HeroName}. The Hetman will no doubt consider this a political maneuver, and he wouldn't be entirely wrong about that-- but the Forlorn <i>do</i>  present a problem to the Compound. He'll listen to you."
// TaskTitle :
"P1828192145" "<color deepskyblue>Abused and Scorned Tho' We May Be</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P470366156" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Saber-Rattling</color>"

