// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P583241119" "Forlorn Guard"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2275253406" "Hello there son"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3790498998" "For all the Hetman's warnings against them being monsters, the Forlorn were willing to speak to you peacefully. You were even offered the choice of interviewing the captured recon soldiers without intereference. This only proves that Anna's intuition is correct: the Forlorn <i>can</i> be reasoned with... without resorting to violence."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P668674209" "That didn't go well at all. For all the Hetman's warnings against them being monsters, though, the Forlorn were willing to speak to you peacefully. You were even offered the choice of interviewing the captured recon soldiers without intereference. This only proves that Anna's intuition is correct: the Forlorn <i>can</i> be reasoned with... without resorting to violence. But it did and all of the recon soldiers suffered for it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3722833648" "Report Your Findings to the Hetman"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2714976274" "{HeroName}, I'm sure what you found in the tunnels is interesting, but we'll speak of it later. Tell the Hetman what you know. He needs to feel secure that we are working with him, not around him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3086736220" "You gave the Hetman your report regarding his lost recon patrol. He made it clear once again that he's no fan of Anna Palatine."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBeginFlashback 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1958742713" "So the Forlorn were willing to speak with you? Even after the Hetman antagonzied them so? That bodes well for any future alliance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DemetriosDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskOwnerPage Text :
"P3114591504" "<color orange>Only your task owner may speak to Demetrios</color>"
// Page DemetriosTalks Text :
"P1009460327" "The Hetman of the Compound has stepped up his game, I see. You're no ordinary kill team."
// Answer Text :
"P3051410299" "The Hetman didn't send me, the Palatine did. And I'm here to strike a truce."
// Page TrucePage Text :
"P690324915" "The Palatine, eh..? I've heard of her. Is there some discontent in the rulership of the Compound? Some of you want to kill us, others to strike an accord. How nice.<br><br>Go back and tell your Palatine that I will have none of it. And tell your Hetman I will eventually wear his neck-veins as a favorite bracelet.<br><br><i>Do you topsiders even know what the Forlorn have done for you?</i>  We are keeping the <color red>Ghouls</color> back from being able to access the surface! If it weren't for the efforts of my people, your Compound would've been overrun by my feral cousins ages ago!"
// Answer Text :
"P3438910048" "On behalf of the Palatine, I thank you for your efforts. She had no idea."
// Page ThanksPage Text :
"P3669116059" "She can thank us by killing the Hetman."
// Answer Text :
"P2951385300" "She'd like to thank you by offering you a Genetic Resequencer instead."
// Page WhatAboutThisPage Text :
"P2969970328" "...<br><br>If your Palatine can pull that off, she will have the support of the Forlorn. And if you are <i>truly</i> here on her behalf, then there is something else I will demand. The Ghouls have somehow breached this tunnel section's outer containment gates. My second, Noble Savage, is leading the charge to reseal them, but he needs help. <color orange>Help Savage seal the outer gates</color> and you shall have your accord."
// Answer Text :
"P1480753600" "It will be done."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1265338882" "Something doesn't quite sit right with me, {HeroName}, not after your last sojourn into the tunnels of the Forlorn. The Hetman may have <i>said</i> that his impetus for sending a recon patrol into their territories was to guage the potential threat of the Forlorn...but your report said the 'recon patrol' had orders to just go in and start shooting. That sounds like a kill team, not reconnaissance, and it doesn't add up. Furthermore, it endangers any chance we have at forming an alliance with the Forlorn.<br><br><color orange>I need you to speak with the leader of the Forlorn, Demetrios Vasilikos, on my behalf as Palatine of the Compound, and see if some kind of truce can be salvaged from all of this.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P2049888074" "We need an olive branch. The Forlorn has no real reason to trust the Compound."
// SendOffString :
"P1853757852" "You're quite right, my friend, which is why <color orange>I will deliver to them a Genetic Resequencer if they will agree to a truce</color>. The Forlorn will be able to cure their feral cousins with such a device, and that is something I know Demetrios wants dearly.<br><br>Mistress Nadia and some of my Shepherds have managed to contact <color yellow>Dr. Helix</color>, who has agreed to come to First Ward if the Carnival can assure her a measure of protection. We're still working on that part, but the Hetman's watchful eye is making things difficult."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P111758147" "Strike an accord with the Forlorn"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1320190432" "Why did you leave the Forlorn tunnels before your mission was done? You must go back."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2772888888" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Sweet Mercy</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P862919935" "Demetrios is just up ahead. He seems pensive."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// KeyClue - PerimeterKeyClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1298790543" "Perimeter Key"
// DetailString :
"P81254920" "You retrieved the perimeter key from Demetrios Vasilikos, leader of the Forlorn."
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - PlayTogetherMission 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3101635437" "Speak With Demetrios"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3560206100" "Help Noble Savage seal the gates"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3337407395" "Manslayer"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P1746038549" "Noble Savage"
// Script Variable PET_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3075588892" "<shout>The feral Ghouls have breached the outer gates in the back of the tunnels! We need to seal them up!"
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P3329747481" "<shout>Is that all you can do?"
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3197159679" "<shout>Engaging biometric scans and safeguards."
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1344494427" "<shout>My biometrics are hitting their warning zones!"
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3092775311" "<shout>My biometrics are failing!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P2045809852" "<shout>Complete biometrics rupture. Entering sleepmode."
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1127431811" "Hello, {HeroName}."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2549984033" "<shout>There's a lot of my feral cousins between us and those outer gate seals! Get ready!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2070580031" "<shout>The left outer gate controls should be nearby!<t 2><t 3>We have to activate these and the ones on the right side for the outer gates to seal!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P292908167" "<shout>We've got outer gate controls on this side!<t 2><t 3>Both sets have to activated before the outer gates actually seal!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2731837394" "Demetrios Vasilikos"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYINFO :
"P198002230" "Leader of the Forlorn"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3255702063" "More visitors from topside, eh?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P894259060" "The Hetman of the Compound has stepped up his game, I see. You're no ordinary kill team.<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P440215301" "Go back and tell your Palatine that I will have no truce. And tell your Hetman I will eventually wear his neck-veins as a favorite bracelet. Do you topsiders even know what the Forlorn have done for you? We are keeping the Ghouls back from being able to access the surface!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1583674261" "Your Palatine can thank us by killing the Hetman.<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2498802441" "A Genetic Resequencer? If your Palatine can pull that off, she will have the support of the Forlorn. But there is something else I demand. The Ghouls have breached these tunnels. Help Noble Savage seal the outer gates.<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4243661427" "We can't hold them back!"
// Script Variable BOSS_TWO_DISPLAYNAME :
"P62836177" "Forlorn Soldier"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2129621104" "They're pouring in from the containment gates!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2101770136" "I can't believe I used to be one of these things!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2005202505" "Someone figured out our containment codes!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2111419698" "Help? Down here?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4066277006" "F-Fresh meat again!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2477593683" "We d-d-on't need your help! Just your blood and bones and flesh and RRRARRGH!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2914618253" "The Savage will make eating f-f-f-for d-d-days!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P176873335" "C-c-containing me only makes me want to eat you m-more!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1059198780" "You c-c-can't hold b-back our HUNGER!<t 0.01>"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2200249979" "T-t-time to eat!<t 0.01>"

